.SH NAME
fwd\-config\-set \- Set a configuration value without opening an editor.
.SH HOMEPAGE
\fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd config set
[OPTIONS] {key} [value]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a configuration value without opening an editor.
.PP
Use '--' before values that begin with '-', for example: fwd config set
default_command -- python -m agent
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fP
Write ~/.fwd/config.toml; this is the default scope.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fP
Write ./.fwd/config.toml for this project.
.TP
\fB\-t,\fP \-\-target <str>
Set a target-specific value, which overrides project and user defaults.
